  "summary": "Four studies directly apply graph neural network message passing over relational graphs to customer churn/attrition prediction, and one applies self-attention encoder models to the same topic. [V0193] (Adebayo et al., 2026) achieves the strongest result, reporting AUROC 0.91 on the ChurnBench dataset. [V0194] (Brennan et al., 2018) is a deployment study on the MetroFlow dataset reporting F1=0.63. [V0195] (Chen et al., 2019) evaluates on the Atlas-ICU dataset with accuracy 0.70. [V0196] (Duarte et al., 2020) reports MAE 0.77 on the AgriSat-4 dataset. [V0200] (El-Sayed et al., 2021) applies self-attention encoder models (not GNN) to customer attrition on AgriSat-4, reporting AUROC 0.88; it is included as the fifth-ranked document as it addresses the same topic but uses a different method. All other candidates address unrelated topics (sepsis, battery life, agricultural yield, fraud, wildfire, traffic, protein function) and are excluded.",
